# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Production before #4452 was fixed (#4466): an adaptive
# split may open while a resize is in flight or its undo is pending, so the
# resize neither captures nor fences the split target, and an acknowledged
# write is lost once the registry retires the saga's row. #4478 relaxed the
# hold only once the resize has completed, which the base's SplitBegin admits.
MODULE: NoKeyLostRetainedSplitDuringResize
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a split opens while a resize is in flight, so the resize neither captures nor fences its target
PERTURBS: SplitBegin

--- FIND
    /\ rz \in {"idle", "retired", "purged", "undone"}
    /\ rmap = s1
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: no interlock with an in-flight resize.
    /\ rmap = s1
--- END